{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#cor:pseudo-riemannian-embedding-criterion","title":"cor:pseudo-riemannian-embedding-criterion","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":3558,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#cor:pseudo-riemannian-embedding-criterion","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:pseudo-riemannian-metric]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:pseudo-metric-has-signature]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:embedding-criterion-pointwise]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:bilinear-gradient]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/appendixA#prop:regular-level-set-hypersurface-codim-one]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/appendixA#prop:regular-level-set-tangent-kernel]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"cor:pseudo-riemannian-embedding-criterion","line":6118,"source":"\\begin{corollary}\n\\label{cor:pseudo-riemannian-embedding-criterion}\n\n\\uses{def:pseudo-riemannian-metric, def:pseudo-metric-has-signature, prop:embedding-criterion-pointwise, def:bilinear-gradient, prop:regular-level-set-hypersurface-codim-one, prop:regular-level-set-tangent-kernel}\n\n\n\n\\dcref{ch2:2.71}\n\nLet $(\\bar M,\\bar g)$ have signature $(r,s)$ and let $M=f^{-1}(c)$. If $\\bar g(\\operatorname{grad}f,\\operatorname{grad}f)>0$ on $M$, then $M$ is an embedded pseudo-Riemannian submanifold of signature $(r-1,s)$; if it is negative, the signature is $(r,s-1)$. In both cases $\\operatorname{grad}f$ is normal to $M$.\n\\end{corollary}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{prop:embedding-criterion-pointwise,prop:regular-level-set-hypersurface-codim-one,prop:regular-level-set-tangent-kernel}\n\\sketch Non-null gradient makes $df_p\\ne0$. Propositions \\ref{prop:regular-level-set-hypersurface-codim-one} and \\ref{prop:regular-level-set-tangent-kernel} give an embedded hypersurface with $T_pM=\\ker df_p$. Apply Proposition \\ref{prop:embedding-criterion-pointwise} to $a=df_p$; Lemma \\ref{lem:bilinear-gradient-orthogonal-ker} gives normality.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Corollary</div></section> <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-636f723a70736575646f2d7269656d616e6e69616e2d656d62656464696e672d637269746572696f6e\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Apseudo-riemannian-metric\">↗ def:pseudo-riemannian-metric</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Apseudo-metric-has-signature\">↗ def:pseudo-metric-has-signature</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Aembedding-criterion-pointwise\">↗ prop:embedding-criterion-pointwise</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Abilinear-gradient\">↗ def:bilinear-gradient</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FappendixA%23prop%3Aregular-level-set-hypersurface-codim-one\">↗ prop:regular-level-set-hypersurface-codim-one</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FappendixA%23prop%3Aregular-level-set-tangent-kernel\">↗ prop:regular-level-set-tangent-kernel</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch2:2.71</span></span><p></p>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(\\bar M,\\bar g)$\">$(\\bar M,\\bar g)$</span> have signature <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(r,s)$\">$(r,s)$</span> and let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M=f^{-1}(c)$\">$M=f^{-1}(c)$</span>. If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\bar g(\\operatorname {grad}f,\\operatorname {grad}f)&gt;0$\">$\\bar g(\\operatorname {grad}f,\\operatorname {grad}f)&gt;0$</span> on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span>, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> is an embedded pseudo-Riemannian submanifold of signature <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(r-1,s)$\">$(r-1,s)$</span>; if it is negative, the signature is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(r,s-1)$\">$(r,s-1)$</span>. In both cases <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\operatorname {grad}f$\">$\\operatorname {grad}f$</span> is normal to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Aembedding-criterion-pointwise\">↗ prop:embedding-criterion-pointwise</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FappendixA%23prop%3Aregular-level-set-hypersurface-codim-one\">↗ prop:regular-level-set-hypersurface-codim-one</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FappendixA%23prop%3Aregular-level-set-tangent-kernel\">↗ prop:regular-level-set-tangent-kernel</a> \\sketch Non-null gradient makes <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$df_p\\ne 0$\">$df_p\\ne 0$</span>. Propositions <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FappendixA%23prop%3Aregular-level-set-hypersurface-codim-one\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/appendixA#prop:regular-level-set-hypersurface-codim-one\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-70726f703a726567756c61722d6c6576656c2d7365742d6879706572737572666163652d636f64696d2d6f6e65\">prop:regular-level-set-hypersurface-codim-one</a> and <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FappendixA%23prop%3Aregular-level-set-tangent-kernel\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/appendixA#prop:regular-level-set-tangent-kernel\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-70726f703a726567756c61722d6c6576656c2d7365742d74616e67656e742d6b65726e656c\">prop:regular-level-set-tangent-kernel</a> give an embedded hypersurface with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$T_pM=\\ker df_p$\">$T_pM=\\ker df_p$</span>. Apply Proposition <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Aembedding-criterion-pointwise\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:embedding-criterion-pointwise\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-70726f703a656d62656464696e672d637269746572696f6e2d706f696e7477697365\">17</a> to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$a=df_p$\">$a=df_p$</span>; Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Abilinear-gradient-orthogonal-ker\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:bilinear-gradient-orthogonal-ker\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a62696c696e6561722d6772616469656e742d6f7274686f676f6e616c2d6b6572\">17</a> gives normality. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:embedding-criterion-nondegenerate-pointwise","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pullback-pseudo-metric-bundle","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:pseudo-riemannian-metric","title":"def:pseudo-riemannian-metric","label":"def:pseudo-riemannian-metric"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:pseudo-metric-has-signature","title":"def:pseudo-metric-has-signature","label":"def:pseudo-metric-has-signature"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:embedding-criterion-pointwise","title":"prop:embedding-criterion-pointwise","label":"prop:embedding-criterion-pointwise"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:bilinear-gradient","title":"def:bilinear-gradient","label":"def:bilinear-gradient"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/appendixA#prop:regular-level-set-hypersurface-codim-one","title":"prop:regular-level-set-hypersurface-codim-one","label":"prop:regular-level-set-hypersurface-codim-one"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/appendixA#prop:regular-level-set-tangent-kernel","title":"prop:regular-level-set-tangent-kernel","label":"prop:regular-level-set-tangent-kernel"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prob:level-sets-pseudo-riemannian","title":"prob:level-sets-pseudo-riemannian","label":"prob:level-sets-pseudo-riemannian"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#cor:pseudo-riemannian-embedding-criterion","title":"cor:pseudo-riemannian-embedding-criterion","tex":"\\begin{corollary}\n\\label{cor:pseudo-riemannian-embedding-criterion}\n\n\\uses{def:pseudo-riemannian-metric, def:pseudo-metric-has-signature, prop:embedding-criterion-pointwise, def:bilinear-gradient, prop:regular-level-set-hypersurface-codim-one, prop:regular-level-set-tangent-kernel}\n\n\n\n\\dcref{ch2:2.71}\n\nLet $(\\bar M,\\bar g)$ have signature $(r,s)$ and let $M=f^{-1}(c)$. If $\\bar g(\\operatorname{grad}f,\\operatorname{grad}f)>0$ on $M$, then $M$ is an embedded pseudo-Riemannian submanifold of signature $(r-1,s)$; if it is negative, the signature is $(r,s-1)$. In both cases $\\operatorname{grad}f$ is normal to $M$.\n\\end{corollary}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{prop:embedding-criterion-pointwise,prop:regular-level-set-hypersurface-codim-one,prop:regular-level-set-tangent-kernel}\n\\sketch Non-null gradient makes $df_p\\ne0$. Propositions \\ref{prop:regular-level-set-hypersurface-codim-one} and \\ref{prop:regular-level-set-tangent-kernel} give an embedded hypersurface with $T_pM=\\ker df_p$. Apply Proposition \\ref{prop:embedding-criterion-pointwise} to $a=df_p$; Lemma \\ref{lem:bilinear-gradient-orthogonal-ker} gives normality.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:pseudo-riemannian-metric","title":"def:pseudo-riemannian-metric","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:pseudo-metric-has-signature","title":"def:pseudo-metric-has-signature","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:embedding-criterion-pointwise","title":"prop:embedding-criterion-pointwise","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:bilinear-gradient","title":"def:bilinear-gradient","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/appendixA#prop:regular-level-set-hypersurface-codim-one","title":"prop:regular-level-set-hypersurface-codim-one","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/appendixA#prop:regular-level-set-tangent-kernel","title":"prop:regular-level-set-tangent-kernel","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}